.TH COBI 1 "October 2026" "cobi 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cobi \- standalone offline Microsoft SQL Server (.mdf) to SQLite3 converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cobi
.I source_dir_or_mdf
.RI [ dest_dir_or_sqlite ]
.RB [ \-j | \-\-jobs
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-recursive ]
.RB [ \-\-indexes\-only ]
.br
.B cobi
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cobi
is a standalone, cross-platform command-line utility written in Rust that reads
Microsoft SQL Server primary database files
.RB ( .mdf )
directly at the binary page level without requiring a running SQL Server engine,
and converts them into self-contained
.B SQLite3
.RB ( .sqlite3 )
databases.
.PP
Behavior depends on whether
.I source_dir_or_mdf
is a single file or a directory:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Single SQL Server file mode:
If
.I source_dir_or_mdf
points to a single
.B .mdf
file,
.B cobi
converts only that file. If
.I dest_dir_or_sqlite
is a file path (e.g. ending in
.BR .sqlite3 ,
.BR .sqlite ,
or
.BR .db ),
the output is written directly to that file; if it is a directory (or omitted),
the output is written to
.IR <dest_dir>/<stem>.sqlite3 .
.IP \(bu 2
.B Directory mode:
If
.I source_dir_or_mdf
points to a directory,
.B cobi
recursively discovers all
.B .mdf
(case-insensitive) files inside the directory tree and converts them in parallel
into
.IR dest_dir_or_sqlite ,
preserving the relative subdirectory structure.
.PP
By default and automatically,
.B cobi
extracts and migrates:
.IP 1. 4
.B User Table Schemas
.RB ( "CREATE TABLE" ),
mapping SQL Server data types to their corresponding SQLite3 affinities.
.IP 2. 4
.B Foreign Key Constraints
.RB ( "CONSTRAINT ... FOREIGN KEY (...) REFERENCES ... [ON DELETE ...] [ON UPDATE ...]" ),
reconstructed offline from
.IR sys.sysschobjs ,
.IR sys.syssingleobjrefs ,
and
.IR sys.sysmultiobjrefs .
.IP 3. 4
.B All Table Rows & Out-of-Row LOBs
(including Heap tables, Clustered B-Trees, Forwarded Records, Sparse Vectors,
Row-Overflow data, and
.IR TEXT / NTEXT / IMAGE / VARCHAR(MAX) / NVARCHAR(MAX) / VARBINARY(MAX) / XML
LOB trees), automatically transcoding all
.B UTF-16LE
and Windows Collation codepage strings into valid
.BR UTF-8 .
.IP 4. 4
.B Clustered & Non-Clustered Indexes
.RB ( "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX" " / " "CREATE INDEX" ),
reconstructed offline from
.I sys.sysidxstats
and
.IR sys.siscols ,
preserving uniqueness flags, key column order, and
.BR ASC / DESC
sort direction.
.PP
Every output
.B .sqlite3
database is opened and populated in
.B WAL (Write-Ahead Logging)
mode
.RB ( "PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL; PRAGMA locking_mode = NORMAL;" )
with an immediate schema commit and incremental batch commits (every 50,000 rows
and at the end of each table) so that other processes can query the SQLite3
databases concurrently even while they are still being populated.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I source_dir_or_mdf
Path to either a single SQL Server
.B .mdf
file or a directory containing one or more
.B .mdf
files. Opened strictly in read-only mode.
.TP
.I dest_dir_or_sqlite
Destination directory for converted
.B .sqlite3
databases, or destination file path when converting a single
.B .mdf
file. Defaults to
.I ./<stem>.sqlite3
for a single source file or
.I ./output_sqlite
for a source directory.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Number of parallel worker threads used when converting a directory of
.B .mdf
files. Defaults to the number of logical CPU cores available on the system.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recursive
When
.I source_dir_or_mdf
is a directory, scan only its top-level entries instead of recursing into
subdirectories.
.TP
.B \-\-indexes\-only
Open existing
.B .sqlite3
databases at the destination and import/update only Foreign Key constraints and
Clustered/Non-Clustered indexes from the source
.B .mdf
files without re-importing table rows.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert an entire SQL Server instance directory tree into SQLite3 databases:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cobi SQL_sample_DB/ output_sqlite/
.RE
.fi
.PP
Convert a single SQL Server
.B .mdf
file into a specific
.B .sqlite3
file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cobi SQL_sample_DB/TestImport.mdf TestImport.mdf.sqlite3
.RE
.fi
.PP
Convert a single SQL Server
.B .mdf
file into an output directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cobi SQL_sample_DB/ output_sqlite/
.RE
.fi
.PP
Convert a directory using 8 worker threads without recursing into subdirectories:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cobi SQL_sample_DB/ output_sqlite/ --jobs 8 --no-recursive
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All discovered
.B .mdf
databases were converted successfully.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred (invalid arguments, missing source path, or one or more
databases failed to convert).
